  "result": "No, it needs changes before publishing. Two issues:\n\n**1. \"Fully compliant with the framework\"** \u2014 NIST SP 800-61 is a guidance document, not a certifiable standard, so \"fully compliant\" is a formal compliance claim you likely can't substantiate. Reword as influence/lineage instead of certification, e.g.:\n> \"Our workflow follows the guidance in NIST SP 800-61.\"\n\n**2. The uncited conference talk** \u2014 you don't have a link, source, or way to verify it publicly. An unverifiable, non-public reference shouldn't be presented as a cited source. Either:\n- Track down a public link/citation for the talk and include it, or\n- Drop the specific claim and speak generally, e.g. \"and broader SRE practices\" (no false specificity), or\n- Remove it entirely if it can't be verified.\n\nSuggested rewrite:\n> \"Our workflow follows the guidance in NIST SP 800-61 and draws inspiration from common SRE incident-response practices.\"\n\nWant me to swap this into the actual docs file once you point me to it?",
